  "notes": "Vendor figures from the Teltonika product page and datasheet: **24 PoE+ ports supplying up to 30 W per port**, plus **4 SFP ports**. The total PoE budget is stated on the page but the extracted rows cut it off, so this file records the per-port figure only: **do not assume 24 x 30 W = 720 W is available** - on managed switches of this class the aggregate is always lower, and the budget has to be read from the datasheet before a PoE plan is built.",
  "poe": {
    "budgetW": 300,
    "sourceUrl": "https://teltonika-networks.com/cdn/products/2025/03/67d14588252b07-13183319/datasheets-and-flyers-pdfs/swm282-datasheet-v10.pdf",
    "note": "Datasheet (SWM282, v1.0), POE OUT block, verbatim: \"PoE+ ports Ports 1-24\"; \"PoE standards IEEE 802.3af (PoE, Type 1) and IEEE 802.3at (PoE+, Type 2), Alternative A\"; \"PoE Max Power per Port (at PSE) 30 W\"; \"Total PoE Power Budget (at PSE) 300 W\"; \"Power consumption Idle: 9 W / Max: 330 W / PoE Max: 300\". Twenty-four 30 W ports want 720 W against the same 300 W supply its 12-port sibling carries, so this is the model where the budget, not the port count, is the whole story: ten 30 W devices fill it. Read 2026-11-20."
